    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d700">

                <pb facs="0786" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1516: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-09T20:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1920—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 10—5:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your cable May 6, 6 p.m.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d700-f1"/> Impossible to give a
                    correct estimate balance sheet Chinese Eastern. Approximately road owes not to
                        <pb facs="0787" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/> exceed five million. But there is
                    due from Allies six million for military transport. Road has been kept going
                    partly by income from operation derived by reason of an exorbitant tariff, from
                    special privileges granted, from a loan of one million from the Chinese
                    Government, by some relatively small payments for military transport, by the use
                    of Allied fund, and by not paying all of its bills.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d700-f1" n="43" xml:id="d700-f1-content">
                <p>“What is financial condition of Chinese Eastern Railway and how have its expenses
                    been met during past six months?” (File no. 861.77/1515a.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
